  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="32207719-3e72-5d21-b7c1-a731ffc02d29" activityNameId="c430e996-5fea-5d18-bf23-aa1c8af0264e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Biogas purification, to methane, 97 vol-%, glycol washing process</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Biogas purification, to methane, 97 vol-%, glycol washing process
Inventory refers to 1 m3 of methane. Electricity consumption and emissions represent the raw gas compression, H2S removal, gas conditioning and methane enrichment of biogas.  The  disposal of activated carbon is neglected.  Infrastructure expenditures are included employing generic data for facilities of a chemical plant as approximation.;
Synonyms: Selexol, Genosorb; 
UUID: a38d2cb9-2390-3c27-9244-657f01f19ac6
Emissions due to leakage and purification of biogas. Input of energy and auxiliary materials. Biogas input excluded from the dataset.
Location: Data represents conditions of biogas purification plants in Switzerland. Energy and material consumption data are from two Swiss operators. Emissions from leakage are calculated.
Technology: Glycol washing using Gensorob as washing agent.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 450 m3/h in Switzerland in 2010
Sampling: Literature data, personal communication 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a38d2cb9-2390-3c27-9244-657f01f19ac6.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
